<title>UK: Sema wins bid for British Rail business unit.</title>
<headline>Sema wins bid for British Rail business unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-French technology company SEMA Group Plc said on Friday British Railways Board approved its bid for BR Business Systems Ltd, a company formed to take over British Rail's business services division.</p>
<p>Sema said BRBSL designs and operates the main railway information technology infrastructure for Britain, including ticketing, asset management, timetabling and other services.</p>
<p>The company has around 1,100 staff and had net assets of 13.2 million pounds as of October 12 last year, Sema said.</p>
<p>Sema said it expected the formal agreement to be signed and the acquisition completed within the next two weeks.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
